	(text
		""
		(at 20 28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d6278f77-ffe7-52a5-9037-0a6eac5a0fcc")
	)
	(text
		"J1 pin 1 = +5 V, pin 2 = GND. Mates with JST XHP-2 housing."
		(at 20 32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7ee384b8-14f3-5c40-8b34-8f532959bacd")
	)
	(text
		"Order: fuse first (fault current meets a limiter), diode second (reversed supply meets a blocker)."
		(at 20 34.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3bb6ab64-24c1-5f6e-a826-a5054f00c815")
	)
	(text
		"D4 clamps transients on +5V_PROT, behind D1 so a reversed supply never forward-biases it."
		(at 20 37.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "632dfc1f-26e0-59de-88ba-148eef2950d8")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 20 39.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1b3e460f-9530-5611-87ef-99e26d743ca0")
	)
	(text
		"AMS1117 tab is VOUT (pin 2): the tab pad is the +3V3 copper area."
		(at 20 43.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "67b49bb8-5d2c-5154-a2cf-8aa1c647ac12")
	)
	(text
		"Power LED (Lite-On LTST-C190KGKT, VF 1.9 to 2.4 V at 20 mA): (3.3 V - 2.4 V) / 680 R = 1.3 mA up to (3.3 V - 1.9 V) / 680 R = 2.1 mA."
		(at 20 46.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d295b2c1-7df2-580a-87dc-7eac16fd9bf8")
	)
	(text
		"Load budget on +3V3: 100 mA maximum (the regulator is rated 1 A)."
		(at 20 48.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ddedca31-f267-54f5-8a77-d1894eeae4a7")
	)
	(text
		"Dissipation P = (Vin - Vout) x I, with Vin taken as 5.0 V (the JST input, before the fuse and the Schottky D1): P = (5.0 - 3.3) x 0.100 A = 0.17 W at the 100 mA budget and 0.51 W at 300 mA, under the 600 mW SOT-223 limit."
		(at 20 51.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "56ead586-dd7d-5d17-8130-f4034f4997ea")
	)
	(text
		"Junction rise = P x thetaJA, with thetaJA = 150 C/W for the SOT-223 (AMS1117 datasheet, Slkor-published copy): 0.17 W x 150 = 25.5 C at 100 mA and 0.51 W x 150 = 76.5 C at 300 mA. With the 125 C junction limit the ambient may reach 99 C at 100 mA and 48 C at 300 mA. Synth's W-SYNTH-THERMAL-001 estimate (1360 mW) comes from the declared load sum."
		(at 20 53.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1c1d674f-9d72-5f7a-9c22-dd3e4a82bf9d")
	)
	(text
		"Dropout is 1.3 V typical and 1.4 V maximum at 1 A (datasheet). With 5.0 V less the drops of F1 and D1 at the regulator, a 4.75 V supply leaves the +3V3 rail between 3.1 V and 3.3 V, inside the supply range of the MCU (2.0 to 3.6 V) and the BME680 (1.71 to 3.6 V)."
		(at 20 56.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d2425a07-1b40-5f0d-855a-667c484e99d6")
	)
	(text
		"Output capacitor: the datasheet asks for at least 10 uF of tantalum with an ESR not above 0.5 ohm. C3 is 47 uF tantalum (ESR 1 ohm per its LCSC listing) with the 10 uF ceramic C4 and the 100 nF C5 in parallel."
		(at 20 58.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "dd60cd4c-f130-5a56-96df-14e49be56d33")
	)
	(text
		"Ceramic capacitance falls with DC bias: C4 (10 uF 0805) is taken at 50 % and 30 % of nominal (5 uF and 3 uF); the 47 uF tantalum C3 meets the 10 uF minimum alone."
		(at 20 61.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "823b7053-1077-541a-b6cb-3dfa424de90e")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 20 63.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1317a226-ae58-5491-98d2-d7f5347a012d")
	)
	(text
		"J4: 1 = 3V3_REF (sense only), 2 = SWDIO, 3 = SWCLK, 4 = GND, 5 = NRST."
		(at 20 67.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "28fbc33c-0796-5750-8b05-2e1acd91ca9e")
	)
	(text
		"PA14 is SWCLK and BOOT0. Default option bytes (nBOOT_SEL=1) ignore the pin; blank flash enters the ROM bootloader. There is no BOOT0 strap on this board."
		(at 20 70.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "56f07222-8d4f-5b88-9976-55c2d7264523")
	)
	(text
		"D8/D9 (SWDIO/SWCLK) and D19 (NRST) are 3.3 V zeners, cathode on the signal, anode on GND; a 5 V clamp would exceed the STM32 input maximum."
		(at 20 73.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f1d2e765-2c17-5feb-b876-d76abfb6fdd4")
	)
	(text
		"Fault current: a 5 V fault on SWDIO/SWCLK through R13/R14 (100R): (5 - 3.3) / 100 = 17 mA, and 24 V is not expected. A 500 mW SOD-123 zener carries that (about 56 mW). NRST has the 10k pull-up and 1k DTR path: (5 - 3.3) / 1k = 1.7 mA."
		(at 20 75.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "318b85c0-13f9-5c5b-9582-6bce5546187a")
	)
	(text
		"Caveat: a 3.3 V zener leaks near its knee at the 3.3 V rail; the leakage into NRST (10k pull-up) and the SWD lines (100R) depends on the zener's datasheet leakage at 3.3 V: needs sourcing (the registry part has no MPN yet)."
		(at 20 78.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7e3cdd28-c940-5fba-bf1f-a7ba10a45c3d")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 20 80.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "880c03ae-a518-51de-a206-587a5f6be1d8")
	)
	(text
		"BME680 SDO low = 0x76, CSB high = I2C. 24LC256 A2:A0 low = 0x50. No collision."
		(at 20 84.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4280eba6-3def-58dc-90a8-c376392810cf")
	)
	(text
		"One pull-up pair, 4.7k each, for the whole bus."
		(at 20 87.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b486934c-c87a-53aa-957c-e212884fdadc")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 20 89.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5f5d2aea-0bd9-5b94-bb09-be137f0cc43f")
	)
	(text
		"J3: 1 GND, 2 UART_TX (MCU out), 3 UART_RX (MCU in), 4 3V3_REF (sense only, 3 mA max)."
		(at 20 93.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4ff187f5-848c-5dbf-9833-56b669801a94")
	)
	(text
		"Host must use 3.3 V logic. D7 (TX) and D24 (RX) are 3.3 V zeners, cathode on the MCU side of the series resistor, anode on GND."
		(at 20 96.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2330fefd-4b2b-55c1-b18d-d5291b02fb73")
	)
	(text
		"Fault current with a 5 V host line on J3: TX (5 - 3.3) / 330 = 5.2 mA, zener power 3.3 V x 5.2 mA = 17 mW; RX (5 - 3.3) / 1k = 1.7 mA, 5.6 mW. A 12 V fault on TX would be (12 - 3.3) / 330 = 26 mA, 86 mW in the zener and 0.23 W in R11, which exceeds an 0603 rating (0.1 W typical, needs sourcing): the connector is specified for 3.3 V to 5 V only."
		(at 20 98.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0b21cf43-b04d-5fa3-ae82-28d465c81252")
	)
	(text
		"The MCU pin sees the zener clamp (3.3 V at the zener test current, datasheet value needs sourcing), below the STM32G030 absolute maximum of VDD + 4 V = 7.3 V (datasheet figure, needs sourcing)."
		(at 20 101.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d34a0db8-effa-5dca-be14-2d155ab38873")
	)
	(text
		"Open: a 3.3 V zener conducts at its knee near 3.3 V, so leakage into the UART lines at logic-high is needs sourcing from the zener datasheet (registry part has no MPN)."
		(at 20 103.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "22439b19-927b-58a7-98ee-d54fdf7bef60")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 20 106.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "bb74455e-5d5a-540e-88af-d8a13b313a56")
	)
	(text
		"J5: 1 3V3_REF, 2 GND, 3 PA0, 4 PA1, 5 PA4, 6 GND, 7 PA5, 8 PA6, 9 PA7, 10 GND, 11 PB0, 12 PB9."
		(at 20 110.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "cba78d69-b57c-5779-bf5a-696c845528f7")
	)
	(text
		"3V3_REF = +3V3 through D14 (blocks back-drive) and 100R: sense or reference only, 3 mA max (about 2.7 V at 3 mA), 30 mA into a short."
		(at 20 112.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7ad476a4-5526-5fc7-9cdf-191d6e1ad5e7")
	)
	(text
		"D10..D13 and D20..D23 are eight 3.3 V zeners, one per GPIO line, cathode on the MCU side of the 330R series resistor, anode on GND."
		(at 20 115.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c1dcdbf4-f193-575e-ab00-48b866bed19c")
	)
	(text
		"Fault current with a 5 V source on a header pin: (5 - 3.3) / 330 = 5.2 mA, zener power 3.3 V x 5.2 mA = 17 mW, resistor power 5.2 mA squared x 330 = 8.9 mW. A 12 V fault is 26 mA, 86 mW zener and 0.23 W in the 0603 resistor (0.1 W typical, needs sourcing): the header is specified for 3.3 V to 5 V only."
		(at 20 118.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8a492441-387c-5f28-960b-32962d84cbe1")
	)
	(text
		"Zener leakage at logic-high near 3.3 V and ADC input error from it (PA0, PA1, PA4, PA6, PA7, PB0 are analog-capable): needs sourcing from the zener datasheet."
		(at 20 120.58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a8585823-620d-5cd2-831a-1ef8292ac677")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 20 123.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c6eeb372-464d-539d-b508-9078e1ceb0c9")
	)
	(text
		"H2, H3: two M2.5 non-plated mounting holes at opposite (diagonal) corners."
		(at 20 127.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8c22047c-791c-5239-8f65-8baafeb2d58d")
	)
